edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536073 true] [17592186382350 1100 "A series RCL circuit has a source electromotive force (EMF) of $8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\,\\text{V},$ a resistance of $24\\,Ω,$ a capacitance of $0.05\\,\\text{F},$ and an inductance of $L=4\\,\\text{H}.$ Find the differential equation governing the amount of charge $q$ (in coulombs) on the capacitor at time $t$ (in seconds).\n\n*Hint: The voltage drop ${V}_{C}$ across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C},$ where $C$ is the capacitance measured in Farads.*" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382350 1113 #uuid "baba8f77-9934-50a4-96a3-21fe5cd03d1c" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382350 1145 "We have the following circuit diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14075717/assets/6494f1905ab90cb3d5655aaa824726255dc7332841ec656dc88c2180b0f93a1c.png)\n\nThe current $I,$ measured in amperes, is defined as the rate of flow of charge $q,$ measured in coulombs.\n\n$$\nI=\\frac{dq}{dt}\n$$\n\nKirchhoff's voltage law states that in a series circuit, the source voltage (EMF) equals the sum of the voltage drops.\n\nIn an RCL circuit, there are three voltage drops:\n\n- The voltage drop across the resistor is proportional to the current, with a constant of proportionality $R=24\\,Ω.$ So,\n\n$$\n{V}_{R}=24I=24\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}.\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{V}_{C}=\\frac{q}{C}=\\frac{q}{0.05}=20q.\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the inductor is proportional to the rate of change of current, with a constant of proportionality $L=4\\,\\text{H}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=4\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}=4\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dq}{dt})=4\\,\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, the differential equation governing the amount of charge $q$ on the capacitor is\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)=24\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+20q+4\\,\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+6\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+5q=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t).\n$$" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382352 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382353 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382354 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382355 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382356 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1041 "selection" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382356 13194139536073 true] [17592186382351 1110 #uuid "a268e6af-30b3-58c9-835c-003904af5fad" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382352 1034 "\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+5q=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536073 true] [17592186382352 1111 #uuid "f6f558e2-fab8-5863-8f5b-ec84ab9a5a32" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382353 1034 "\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+6\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+5q=2" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536073 true] [17592186382353 1111 #uuid "d4beda4a-abef-5700-8c93-44ec3a8e477c" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382354 1034 "\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+6\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+\\frac{1}{5}q=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536073 true] [17592186382354 1111 #uuid "9afcf8e8-5326-50a0-a1a7-1cd55f2cdb6e" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382355 1034 "\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+6\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+5q=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536073 true] [17592186382355 1111 #uuid "3bd9e059-04a4-5633-b1e5-d36697d804dd" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382356 1034 "\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+6\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+5q=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)" 13194139536073 true] [17592186382356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536073 